WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.588 --> 00:00:16.412
The man walked into the Tang Monk’s room.

2
00:00:16.432 --> 00:00:18.833
“Wh-who are you?”

3
00:00:19.293 --> 00:00:21.053
asked the Tang Monk nervously.

4
00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:25.475
“I’m king of the Black Rooster Kingdom,” said the man.

5
00:00:25.495 --> 00:00:29.576
“My kingdom suffered a horrible drought five years ago.

6
00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.486
Crops wouldn’t grow, and my people were starving.

7
00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:37.768
One day a Daoist arrived in the kingdom.

8
00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:41.831
He said he had great powers and could pray for rain.”

9
00:00:41.851 --> 00:00:45.433
“Did the Daoist’s prayers bring rain?”

10
00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:46.734
asked the Tang Monk.

11
00:00:47.795 --> 00:00:48.576
The king nodded.

12
00:00:48.596 --> 00:00:52.298
“It rained for days, and our crops began to grow.”

13
00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:56.261
“Wonderful!” said the Tang Monk with a smile.

14
00:00:56.941 --> 00:00:58.602
But then his smile faded.

15
00:00:58.622 --> 00:01:00.544
“I’m confused.

16
00:01:01.108 --> 00:01:02.148
Why do you need my help?”

17
00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:05.789
The king took a deep breath.

18
00:01:05.809 --> 00:01:10.151
“After the Daoist brought the rain, we became close friends.

19
00:01:11.411 --> 00:01:15.332
One day we were walking when I noticed a strange light coming from my well.

20
00:01:16.432 --> 00:01:17.933
I went to the well and looked in.

21
00:01:18.893 --> 00:01:21.034
Suddenly I felt someone push me in.

22
00:01:23.675 --> 00:01:25.075
It was the Daoist!

23
00:01:25.835 --> 00:01:28.596
He had made the light with magic so he could trick me.

24
00:01:29.916 --> 00:01:33.397
I fell deep into the water, and he sealed the well shut.”

25
00:01:36.518 --> 00:01:38.338
Tears came to the king’s eyes.

26
00:01:38.358 --> 00:01:41.479
“My body is still down there.

27
00:01:42.499 --> 00:01:43.260
I’m just a...

28
00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.501
ghost.” “That’s horrible!”

29
00:01:46.781 --> 00:01:47.721
said the Tang Monk.

30
00:01:47.741 --> 00:01:50.202
“Your guards punished the Daoist, right?”

31
00:01:51.162 --> 00:01:52.262
The king shook his head.

32
00:01:52.282 --> 00:01:58.884
“The Daoist made himself look like me, and now everyone thinks he’s the real king.”

33
00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.181
The king paused.

34
00:02:01.201 --> 00:02:04.544
“I’ve been in the Land of Darkness ever since.

35
00:02:06.485 --> 00:02:08.587
Tonight a spirit brought me to see you.

36
00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:10.609
He said you can help me.”

37
00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:13.031
“How can I help you?”

38
00:02:13.311 --> 00:02:14.252
asked the Tang Monk.

39
00:02:15.032 --> 00:02:15.873
“I’m just a monk.”

40
00:02:18.335 --> 00:02:21.437
“Yes, but you’re traveling with Sun Wukong,” said the king.

41
00:02:21.457 --> 00:02:24.180
“Sun Wukong is very powerful.

42
00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.902
He can destroy the Daoist!”

43
00:02:27.883 --> 00:02:29.384
The Tang Monk hesitated.

44
00:02:30.472 --> 00:02:33.655
“Wukong can’t charge into the palace and attack the Daoist.

45
00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:38.519
People will think the monkey is evil, attacking a king for no reason.”

46
00:02:38.539 --> 00:02:44.124
“My son, the prince, can bring all of you into the palace,” said the king.

47
00:02:44.144 --> 00:02:48.187
“Then Sun Wukong can fight the Daoist in private.”

48
00:02:48.207 --> 00:02:50.529
“Where can we find the prince?”

49
00:02:51.029 --> 00:02:51.650
asked the monk.

50
00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.134
“He will be out hunting tomorrow,” said the king.

51
00:02:56.154 --> 00:02:58.476
“Tell him everything I told you.”

52
00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.682
“But he won’t believe us,” said the monk.

53
00:03:01.702 --> 00:03:04.224
“He thinks that Daoist is his father.”

54
00:03:04.244 --> 00:03:06.406
“Show him this.”

55
00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.148
The king held up a jade coin.

56
00:03:09.168 --> 00:03:12.691
“This is the one royal treasure I still have.

57
00:03:13.511 --> 00:03:15.933
When my son sees it, he’ll know you’re telling the truth.”

58
00:03:17.014 --> 00:03:18.896
Suddenly the king looked at the door.

59
00:03:18.916 --> 00:03:21.098
“The spirit is calling me.

60
00:03:21.638 --> 00:03:22.198
I must go.”

61
00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:23.840
The king vanished.

62
00:03:25.952 --> 00:03:29.476
The Tang Monk called to his companions, who rushed into the room.

63
00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:34.620
The monk told them everything that the king had said.

64
00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.184
“He showed me a jade coin,” said the monk.

65
00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:39.925
He looked around.

66
00:03:39.945 --> 00:03:42.248
“I don’t know where it is now though.”

67
00:03:42.268 --> 00:03:46.251
“It was just a dream,” said Wukong.

68
00:03:46.272 --> 00:03:50.636
“No, it wasn’t a dream,” said the monk, still looking around.

69
00:03:54.164 --> 00:03:56.005
He went outside, and the others followed.

70
00:03:56.025 --> 00:03:57.865
“There it is!”

71
00:03:58.725 --> 00:04:01.366
A jade coin lay on the ground by the door.

72
00:04:04.687 --> 00:04:07.128
The next morning the prince went out hunting.

73
00:04:10.448 --> 00:04:12.769
He saw a white rabbit and shot an arrow.

74
00:04:13.589 --> 00:04:15.210
He missed and the rabbit ran.

75
00:04:20.431 --> 00:04:23.372
The prince chased the rabbit as it ran into a monastery.

76
00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:28.544
Inside, the prince saw a monk, a pig, and a purple spirit.

77
00:04:29.725 --> 00:04:31.587
Then the rabbit turned into a monkey.

78
00:04:31.607 --> 00:04:34.409
“What’s going on here?”

79
00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:35.390
cried the prince.

80
00:04:36.411 --> 00:04:37.672
The monk stepped forward.

81
00:04:37.692 --> 00:04:39.794
“Don’t be scared, Prince.

82
00:04:40.415 --> 00:04:41.516
We must tell you something.”
